{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1184976-a-great-dilemma","id":1184976,"title":"A great dilemma","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-11T18:50:09-08:00","id":1184976,"title":"A great dilemma","content":"I need your help people because I got stuck between a metaphysical rock and a hard place... In a time traveling chronicle I'm currently leading, an archmaster is trying to rewrite history as we, and the players, know it... they managed to form a plan to defeat the Big Bad\u2122 during the earliest era in Dark Eras and history was saved... or so I thought. One of my more devious players formulated a plan and I'm not sure if I should let it happen or not. Its a damn good plan, with a lot of dangers, and probably it could work, but I'm not sure about consequences of it, so I'm asking for advice.<br /> In the chronicle, the player in question achieved archmastery and stopped the Big Bad\u2122 before the Sundering... before returning to present, he and the rest of the players found a remnant of Time Before. And then they came up with a plan to go there/then/way back when in Time Before through the anomaly. The arch mage has archmastery of both Time and Space Arcanum and wants to go in. To scry into the past of the shard of Time Before and enter it...<br /> I think it's going to end bad, but the idea of going back sounds so damn good. What I'm asking is, is it possible mechanics-wise and if it is, where/when will they arrive and how to present/describe to them the Time Before? Any advice or information I should look for in one of the books? I got caught completely by surprise and I don't want to outright say no to them...<br /> So... any advice or help is welcomed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T20:20:35-08:00","id":1185004,"title":"","content":"The general agreement is that if it involves archmastery, it\u2019s possible. If not now, then sooner or later. At this point, that one player is working on a completely different game - where others are playing wizards and witches, they\u2019re playing demigods and archangels. <br /> <br /> As to presenting the Time Before... it hugely depends on what you and your table hold canon. It\u2019s the ultimate \u201cHere be dragons\u201d territory for the Awakened. I personally favor giving it an Exalted feel (or at least, the stereotypes regarding Exalted). Whatever you end up doing, though, it\u2019ll be nice to include something that flat-out contradicts standard mages\u2019 understanding of the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T21:19:04-08:00","id":1185011,"title":"","content":"The time before doesn't exists any more, so that would be a huge paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T23:42:27-08:00","id":1185036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1184976-a-great-dilemma#post1184976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need your help people because I got stuck between a metaphysical rock and a hard place... In a time traveling chronicle I'm currently leading, an archmaster is trying to rewrite history as we, and the players, know it... they managed to form a plan to defeat the Big Bad\u2122 during the earliest era in Dark Eras and history was saved... or so I thought. One of my more devious players formulated a plan and I'm not sure if I should let it happen or not. Its a damn good plan, with a lot of dangers, and probably it could work, but I'm not sure about consequences of it, so I'm asking for advice.<br /> In the chronicle, the player in question achieved archmastery and stopped the Big Bad\u2122 before the Sundering... before returning to present, he and the rest of the players found a remnant of Time Before. And then they came up with a plan to go there/then/way back when in Time Before through the anomaly. The arch mage has archmastery of both Time and Space Arcanum and wants to go in. To scry into the past of the shard of Time Before and enter it...<br /> I think it's going to end bad, but the idea of going back sounds so damn good. What I'm asking is, is it possible mechanics-wise and if it is, where/when will they arrive and how to present/describe to them the Time Before? Any advice or information I should look for in one of the books? I got caught completely by surprise and I don't want to outright say no to them...<br /> So... any advice or help is welcomed...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Time Before is that way due to the Exarchs (probably), so beyond even Archmasters to undo.<br /> <br /> <i>But</i> since you want to anyways, treat it as a larger Pocket Dimension. Making the whole thing a Hallow or Verge might be appropriate too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T00:16:09-08:00","id":1185042,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand it, The Time Before is capital g Gone.<br /> It's not just harder to get to, requiring Archmastery, it's flat up &quot;not a thing&quot; any more, and the Shards of that time found in pre-history are basically just pictures.<br /> <br /> A devoted Archmage could try and climb in one of those pictures, but he'd merely find himself possibly stuck in a shattered chunk of time, an evaporating fragment of a thing that no longer Is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T00:33:11-08:00","id":1185044,"title":"","content":"Echoing what others said and clarifying/ building upon what I said: Make that *shard* of the Time Before (which won\u2019t be the entirety of the Time Before) you enter a singularity in the uinverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T03:25:24-08:00","id":1185076,"title":"","content":"If you have read Demon: the Descent there\u2019s a good example of what the others are talking (A shard of time, though not the Time Before) about in the Seattle setting, and that\u2019s how I\u2019d run it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T03:29:50-08:00","id":1185078,"title":"","content":"The reason behind them believing it (the Time Before) exists intact are the Exarchs. If they hail from that time/place, and that time/place is now gone and never was, shouldn't also Exarchs be gone since the world/universe they were born in is no more. In an example, if I'm from an island, was born there etc. and go back in time and edit reality so that island never was, how can I exist then. The paradox that is Exarchs. So them existing means that somewhere out there is a gateway to the Time Before that is somehow locked away from being accessed. I find logic in their thinking and I kinda like the idea. <br /> <br /> But if it's impossible, then a shard of a Time Before will do. It would be a bitter ending. Them ending up locked in a pocket realm of lies and half truths that is perhaps a pale shadow of what it once was. But how to portray it. The glory of what it once was. Walking never leads you only through space, but even several seconds later or earlier, so you can see yourself. Effect sometimes comes before the cause. Constantly evolving and adapting life forms. Scintillating flames and electricity dancing in the skies among the moon(s) and nebulae.<br /> Or am I wrong, and I'm explaining the Abyss? <br /> <br /> As I said, not sure how to portray it to the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T03:54:25-08:00","id":1185081,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re forgetting how time/reality edits work in Mage. To the world it\u2019s always been that way, in your subjective opinion you went back and changed it. <br /> <br /> Besides, the Exarchs didn\u2019t destroy the universe, they altered it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-12-2018, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T04:24:18-08:00","id":1185092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1184976-a-great-dilemma?p=1185081#post1185081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You\u2019re forgetting how time/reality edits work in Mage. To the world it\u2019s always been that way, in your subjective opinion you went back and changed it.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Exarchs didn\u2019t destroy the universe, they altered it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Where do Exarchs come from? If Awakened City never was? They were always there in our reality? They had to originate somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T04:35:23-08:00","id":1185099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1184976-a-great-dilemma?p=1185092#post1185092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Where do Exarchs come from? If Awakened City never was? They were always there in our reality? They had to originate somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exarchs <i>now</i> have always existed. Maybe that wasn't always the case? But within the timelines of the Phenominal World, their existance is Truth, regardless of source. This is pretty much what Ascension <i>means</i>.<br /> <br /> The Time Before is now just of bunch of magic ruins. Artifacts from prior timelines? Magically created make-believe? They don't exist now, so you can really tell. There isn't even consistancy, so you don't even know which is &quot;true&quot; (if, in fact, any are).<br /> <br /> But since you bring up the Abyss... since it is &quot;what is not&quot;, there <i>may</i> be remnants of the Time Before in it as well. Good luck with the Anunnaki!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T04:35:23-08:00","id":1185100,"title":"","content":"Or, more simply, let them face a certain entity that will probably devour or erase them from existence them should they attempt to do something like that. Like a Cerberus, but on a realm scale.<br /> Harsh lesson in not to mess with things that are far beyond their comprehension, just in case you want to actually save the timeline you are currently in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16351-milanwow123","name":"milanwow123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T04:38:02-08:00","id":1185103,"title":"","content":"Oh, I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> said somewhere that Supernal Magic in the Time Before wasn't like Mages use now (the Supernal not having been cut off by the Abyss and there being no Watchtowers), but was closer to how Archmasters use magic. For whatever that means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T04:47:04-08:00","id":1185107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1184976-a-great-dilemma?p=1185092#post1185092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Where do Exarchs come from? If Awakened City never was? They were always there in our reality? They had to originate somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever heard of a \u201cretcon,\u201d where the writers change canon history/setting in a comic, and make it so that the in-universe setting of the comic has always been that way, without the characters knowing what changed (save for maybe 4th-wall breaking ones like Deadpool)?<br /> <br /> That\u2019s how changes made directly in the Supernal (which include Awakenings, attaining archmastery, and Ascensions) work, in contrast with normal Awakened magic. Hell, even with normal Time magic, you can explicitly prevent yourself from being born and return to a present where nobody knows you. Archmages and Ascended beings (eg. Exarchs) do that to the entire world when they move the Supernal, not just one subject\u2019s timeline. That\u2019s the level of power we\u2019re dealing with here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T05:49:49-08:00","id":1185123,"title":"","content":"Plus the way that Time magic works in Awakenening there's no Grandfather Paradox, you could go back in time, kill your parents as babies and still exist, destroying your home town seems pretty trivial in comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T06:35:10-08:00","id":1185140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1184976-a-great-dilemma?p=1185092#post1185092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do Exarchs come from? If Awakened City never was? They were always there in our reality? They had to originate somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time magic explicitly skips this paradox. The guy who casts the spell that alters the past is himself immune to the effects of the alteration being made. If he kills his parents before they conceive him, he returns to a world where there's no proof that he ever existed, but he himself is unharmed and remembers his life as it actually was before the past had changed.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the Exarchs can come from Time Before even if the Time Before is no more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T07:20:44-08:00","id":1185160,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1191\" data-vbnamecard=\"1191\">Rosencroft</a> Published materials already state that Artifacts and Atlantean Ruins, all elements of the Time Before, exist in defiance of history. Time Spells intended to read their pasts yield nonsensical results. That's because they don't just come from another timeline. They're detached from time entirely. If Fallen Reality is a book with a beginning, middle and end - all susceptible to revisions - the shard of Time Before is a single page torn out from another book. Once you reach the torn edges, it has no past or future, just whatever you can glean from it. An Archmage could possibly graft a new past onto it, but that wouldn't be the genuine article. Mere time travel can't unseat an Exarch, because the Exarchs escaped time entirely, and now exist outside of it. However, the shard may still have clues towards who an Exarch was before Ascending.<br /> <br /> Consider the following:<br /> Once the players go as far as they can into the past, they meet a cliff - time has been torn off at the moment of the Fall. If they look around they meet an old woman - mostly senile. She speaks a language never spoken on Earth, but when has that even been a problem to an enterprising Mage. She's awaiting the return of her son who does very important work off-shore. He left her magic servitors to care for her needs, but she wishes he came to visit more often. However, she knows how busy he must be after the catastrophe. Yes, she's sure he's still alive, he's a Willworker after all. Deep inside she fears he forgot about her but she's old and her bubble of a world so small - hope is all she has left. In her possession is a picture she's eager to show off - as moms do. It's an image of her son wearing the symbol of a prominent Exarch. If the Exarch finds out what the players know, he's bound to be livid at having his humble origins seen. If he sends an Ochema into the shard, the old woman will have a flash of surprise and joy before the Exarch kills her. On they other hand, there may be no reaction from the Exarch. Perhaps he did forget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:19:41-08:00","id":1185245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milanwow123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1184976-a-great-dilemma?p=1185100#post1185100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, more simply, let them face a certain entity that will probably devour or erase them from existence them should they attempt to do something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Release the hounds.<br /> <br /> Of Tindalos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:39:32-08:00","id":1185258,"title":"","content":"Langoliers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T13:49:59-08:00","id":1185333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1184976-a-great-dilemma?p=1185258#post1185258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1133723#post1133723\">Langoliers</a></div> </div> </div> </div>For example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:51:24-08:00","id":1188624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milanwow123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1184976-a-great-dilemma?p=1185100#post1185100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, more simply, let them face a certain entity that will probably devour or erase them from existence them should they attempt to do something like that. Like a Cerberus, but on a realm scale.<br /> Harsh lesson in not to mess with things that are far beyond their comprehension, just in case you want to actually save the timeline you are currently in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm all for not doing this. One thing you don't want to do is punish creativity or curiosity &quot;just because.&quot; Should there be danger? Absolutely; but as a consequence of how The Time Before *is* and why it is hidden- not because they did a no-no / something you didn't foresee and plan for.<br /> <br /> One of your players is an Archmage, and you should respect what that is and what it entails.<br /> <br /> That said, being unprepared is it's own punishment, and bringing along non-Archmages is a bad idea.<br /> <br /> The real danger should be pissing off the Exarchs, and/or violating the Pax Arcanum. The Exarchs scoured The Time Before from the main timeline, and it requires Archmastery to even detect it and enter it. Obviously the Exarchs want it to be left alone. However, weigh the danger against a reward, to make it enticing; there should be at least a few exceptional rewards for entering such a place (i.e. powerful artifacts, hidden grimoires, incredible rotes, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 02-22-2018, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T13:07:31-08:00","id":1188630,"title":"","content":"Edit: Wrong thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 02-22-2018, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}